# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/people_others.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event kael_snowball
# en: Snow in Thawmoon
title [1b8dde] = 融雪月里的雪
# en: It's snowing in the courtyard. Only in a small circle, around Kael, who is holding a snowball and looking at it as though he's never been allowed to throw one.
text [540758] = 庭院里在下雪。只在一小圈范围里，围着凯尔下。他手里捧着一个雪球，盯着它看，好像从来没被允许扔过雪球。
# en: A courtyard where it is snowing in one small circle only, a boy in a fur coat standing at its centre holding a perfect snowball.
scene [8ebdb4] = 庭院里只有一小圈地方在下雪，一个穿毛皮大衣的少年站在中央，捧着一个完美的雪球。
# en: Leave him to it
opt.left.label [b84f2c] = 让他自己待着
# en: When you pass again, the circle of snow is gone, and there's a small, lopsided snowman in its place.
opt.left.say.1 [631d77] = 你再经过时，那圈雪已经不见了，原地立着一个歪歪扭扭的小雪人。
# en: Throw the first one
opt.right.label [c2945e] = 先扔出第一个
# en: Your snowball hits him in the ear. He stares. Then he laughs — a real laugh, startled out of him — and the snow triples.
opt.right.say.1 [5c45fb] = 你的雪球砸中了他的耳朵。他愣愣地看着你。然后他笑了——一声真正的、被吓出来的笑——雪下得大了三倍。

@event kael_cold_hands
# en: Cold Hands
title [a4a2d1] = 冰冷的手
# en: Kael's hands are always cold. In the library tonight they're so cold the ink in his pen has frozen. He's trying to thaw it with his breath, embarrassed.
text [2a76e5] = 凯尔的手总是冰的。今晚在图书馆里，冷到他笔里的墨水都冻住了。他正难为情地往笔上哈气，想把它化开。
# en: Two students sitting close in a library alcove, one holding the other's frost-white hand between both of theirs.
scene [d7ab82] = 图书馆的壁龛里，两个学生挨坐在一起，一人用双手捧着另一人霜白的手。
# en: Lend him your gloves
opt.left.label [7bd15d] = 把手套借给他
# en: He wears them for the rest of the term. They're far too small. He doesn't care. Your own fingers go numb on the walk back.
opt.left.say.1 [6436b9] = 他戴了一整个学期。手套小得离谱。他不在乎。回去的路上，你自己的手指冻得发麻。
# en: Warm his hands in yours
opt.right.label [e4839d] = 用你的手暖他的手
# en: He goes very still. Then, slowly, the frost on his fingertips melts. "Nobody's ever been warm enough," he says quietly. "Before."
opt.right.say.1 [79ec72] = 他一动不动。然后，慢慢地，他指尖的霜融化了。“从来没有人足够温暖，”他轻声说，“在你之前。”

@event kael_confession
# en: Thaw
title [448405] = 解冻
# en: "I was taught not to want things," Kael says. "Wanting things is how they control you." Frost blooms across the window behind him. "I want you. I'm sorry. I don't know what to do with it."
text [6c0866] = “我被教导不要想要任何东西，”凯尔说，“想要东西，他们就能控制你。”他身后的窗户上绽开了霜花。“我想要你。对不起。我不知道该拿它怎么办。”
# en: Frost-ferns spreading across a dark window behind a pale boy who is, for once, looking directly at someone.
scene [992624] = 一个苍白的少年身后，黑暗的窗上蔓延着霜蕨；这一次，他直视着某个人。
# en: Gently say no
opt.left.label [f46b92] = 温柔地拒绝
# en: He nods, as if he expected it. "Thank you for being honest. Nobody is." The frost on the window fades slowly.
opt.left.say.1 [b81eae] = 他点点头，像是早有预料。“谢谢你的诚实。没有人诚实过。”窗上的霜慢慢褪去了。
# en: Show him what to do with it
opt.right.label [6ebbe7] = 告诉他该怎么办
# en: You kiss him. Every window in the corridor frosts over at once, and then, very slowly, melts.
opt.right.say.1 [775fed] = 你吻了他。走廊里所有的窗户一下子都结满了霜，然后，非常非常缓慢地，融化了。

@event bram_intro
# en: Running in the Halls
title [b6d158] = 走廊奔跑
# en: "Running in the halls." A burly prefect with a red sash steps into your path, ledger already open. "Name?" You weren't running. You were walking briskly.
text [db3db6] = “在走廊里奔跑。”一个系着红绶带的魁梧级长挡住你的去路，记过簿已经翻开了。“名字？”你没在跑。你只是走得比较快。
# en: A burly prefect with a red sash blocking a corridor, a demerit ledger open in one hand and a quill poised.
scene [de700d] = 一个系红绶带的魁梧级长堵在走廊里，一手翻开记过簿，羽毛笔蓄势待发。
# en: Accept the demerit
opt.left.label [758a3a] = 接受记过
# en: He writes your name very slowly, enjoying it. Bram Hollis. You will learn to recognise his footsteps.
opt.left.say.1 [67c2a7] = 他非常缓慢地写下你的名字，乐在其中。布拉姆·霍利斯。你会学会辨认他的脚步声的。
# en: Argue
opt.right.label [2f9da9] = 争辩
# en: "Walking briskly," you insist. Two demerits: one for running, one for "lip". Some students nearby clap quietly.
opt.right.say.1 [4c2d1e] = “是快走。”你坚持道。记两次过：一次因为奔跑，一次因为“顶嘴”。附近几个学生悄悄鼓起了掌。

@event bram_hall_tax
# en: The Hall Tax
title [86f712] = 走廊税
# en: Bram has invented a "hall tax" for using the east staircase. Eight crowns. "Maintenance," he says. The first-years are paying. He looks at you expectantly.
text [7f337c] = 布拉姆发明了一种使用东楼梯的“走廊税”。八克朗。“维护费。”他说。一年级生们都在交。他满怀期待地看着你。
# en: A prefect leaning against a stone archway, palm out, a line of nervous first-years shuffling past him.
scene [77c192] = 一名级长靠在石拱门上，摊着手掌，一排紧张的一年级生从他身边挪过。
# en: Pay it
opt.left.label [e4d5d6] = 交钱
# en: He pockets the coins. "Pleasure." You take the west staircase forever after.
opt.left.say.1 [ed6293] = 他把硬币揣进兜里。“荣幸。”从此以后你永远走西楼梯。
# en: Refuse loudly
opt.right.label [c7392c] = 大声拒绝
# en: The first-years stop paying too. Bram is furious. He'll find a way to make you pay later. He always does.
opt.right.say.1 [9b89a4] = 一年级生们也不交了。布拉姆气坏了。他迟早会想办法让你付出代价。他总会的。
# en: Your refusal spreads. Within a week, nobody pays the hall tax. Bram drops it, scowling.
opt.right.say.2 [7da052] = 你的拒绝传开了。不出一周，再也没人交走廊税。布拉姆黑着脸取消了它。

@event bram_sabotage
# en: Missing Notes
title [a08f2a] = 消失的笔记
# en: Two days before exams, your revision notes vanish from your desk. All of them. You saw a red sash in the corridor.
text [bb41e4] = 考试前两天，你的复习笔记从桌上消失了。全部。你在走廊里看见了一抹红绶带。
# en: An empty desk drawer, a few scattered pages on the floor, a red prefect's sash glimpsed disappearing around a corner.
scene [a3c002] = 一只空荡荡的抽屉，地上散落着几页纸，一条红色的级长绶带消失在拐角。
# en: Rewrite them from memory
opt.left.label [429e64] = 凭记忆重写
# en: You rewrite everything in one furious night. Your new notes are better than the old ones. Take that, Bram.
opt.left.say.1 [2171a3] = 你愤怒地熬了一夜，把一切重写了一遍。新笔记比旧的还好。吃瘪吧，布拉姆。
# en: You rewrite what you can. It isn't enough. Exams go worse than they should.
opt.left.say.2 [0f1b73] = 你重写了能记住的部分。不够。考试考得比该有的差。
# en: Search his room
opt.right.label [8fc51c] = 搜他的房间
# en: You find your notes under his mattress, and also a teddy bear. You take both. You return the bear. Eventually.
opt.right.say.1 [7aa561] = 你在他床垫下找到了你的笔记，还有一只泰迪熊。你两样都拿走了。熊你还回去了。最终。
# en: He catches you in his room. That's two weeks of detention, and he gets to supervise.
opt.right.say.2 [297e67] = 他在自己房间里逮住了你。两周禁闭，由他亲自监督。

@event bram_crying
# en: Behind the Stables
title [321daa] = 马厩后面
# en: Behind the stables, you find Bram Hollis sitting on a bucket, crying into a crumpled letter. He sees you and freezes. "If you tell anyone," he begins, but his voice cracks.
text [b7fc13] = 在马厩后面，你发现布拉姆·霍利斯坐在一只水桶上，对着一封揉皱的信哭。他看见你，僵住了。“你要是敢告诉别人——”他开口，声音却哑了。
# en: A big prefect sitting on an upturned bucket behind the stables, a crumpled letter in his fist, shoulders shaking.
scene [a696df] = 一个高大的级长坐在马厩后倒扣的水桶上，拳头里攥着揉皱的信，肩膀在发抖。
# en: Walk away and never mention it
opt.left.label [6b7a64] = 走开，永远不提
# en: You leave. You never tell anyone. Somehow, he knows you didn't. His demerits become fewer.
opt.left.say.1 [27fbd6] = 你走开了。你从没告诉任何人。不知怎么的，他知道你没说。他给你记的过变少了。
# en: Sit down and ask what happened
opt.right.label [bf652a] = 坐下来，问他出了什么事
# en: His father. A letter saying he's a disappointment, again. "He was a prefect too," Bram says. "Head boy. I'm just... loud." He wipes his face. "Don't be nice to me. I don't know what to do with it."
opt.right.say.1 [0fc8cf] = 是他父亲。又一封说他令人失望的信。“他以前也是级长，”布拉姆说，“学生会主席。我只是……嗓门大。”他擦了擦脸。“别对我好。我不知道该拿它怎么办。”

@event bram_turns
# en: An Unexpected Ally
title [fb9811] = 意外的盟友
# en: Two sixth-years corner you by the boathouse, looking for trouble. Then a red sash steps between you. "Problem?" says Bram, cracking his knuckles. They leave fast.
text [68c10e] = 两个六年级生在船屋边把你堵住，想找茬。这时一条红绶带插到了你们中间。“有问题吗？”布拉姆捏着指关节说。那两人很快就走了。
# en: A prefect stepping between a cornered student and a pair of older bullies, arms crossed.
scene [b5e93a] = 一名级长抱着双臂挡在被逼到角落的学生和两个高年级恶霸之间。
# en: Thank him awkwardly
opt.left.label [a37131] = 别扭地道谢
# en: "Don't make it weird," he says, and walks off. He's smiling, slightly.
opt.left.say.1 [bd632c] = “别搞得这么肉麻。”他说完就走了。他在笑，有一点。
# en: Offer your hand
opt.right.label [1f34dd] = 伸出手
# en: He stares at your hand. Then he shakes it, hard. "Fine. Friends. But I'm still giving you demerits." He does. Fewer.
opt.right.say.1 [5c04b4] = 他盯着你的手。然后用力握住。“行吧。朋友。但我照样给你记过。”他照样记。少了些。

@event bram_duel
# en: A Formal Challenge
title [0903a6] = 正式挑战
# en: Bram throws a glove at your feet in front of half the dormitory. "Formal challenge. The dueling green, right now. Unless you're a coward." Everyone is watching.
text [28f81c] = 布拉姆当着半个宿舍的人把一只手套扔在你脚下。“正式挑战。决斗草坪，现在就去。除非你是个懦夫。”所有人都在看。
# en: A white glove lying on a dormitory floor, a red sash folded beside it, a crowd peering through the doorway.
scene [c0de53] = 宿舍地板上一只白手套，旁边叠着一条红绶带，门口挤满了张望的人。
# en: Decline
opt.left.label [eaef39] = 拒绝
# en: "Coward," he says, delighted. It sticks for a while. Then people forget. Mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [821d12] = “懦夫。”他兴高采烈地说。这个外号跟了你一阵子。后来大家就忘了。大体上。
# en: Accept
opt.right.label [b26149] = 接受
# en: You disarm him in three moves. The crowd goes wild. Bram, on the grass, starts laughing. "Fine," he says. "Fine."
opt.right.say.1 [5700d2] = 你三招就缴了他的械。人群沸腾了。躺在草地上的布拉姆笑了起来。“行，”他说，“行。”
# en: He wins. But it takes him a full ten minutes, and he's limping too. He nods to you after. Grudging respect.
opt.right.say.2 [a5c4a7] = 他赢了。但足足花了十分钟，而且他也一瘸一拐的。事后他朝你点了点头。不情不愿的尊重。

@event thorne_intro
# en: The First Question
title [7b3e5e] = 第一个问题
# en: First Arcana lecture. Professor Thorne surveys the room like a hawk over a field of mice. His finger lands on you. "You. What is the first law of the Arcane?"
text [969362] = 第一堂奥术课。索恩教授扫视教室，像一只盯着田鼠的鹰。他的手指落在你身上。“你。奥术第一定律是什么？”
# en: A steep lecture theatre, a stern grey-bearded professor pointing a long finger at one student in the middle row.
scene [662f2a] = 陡峭的阶梯讲堂，一位严厉的灰胡子教授用修长的手指指着中间一排的一个学生。
# en: Admit you don't know
opt.left.label [a10b0e] = 承认你不知道
# en: "Correct answer," he says. "The first law is: know what you don't know. The rest of you, write that down."
opt.left.say.1 [7cfbd1] = “正确答案，”他说，“第一定律是：知道自己不知道什么。其余的人，记下来。”
# en: Take a guess
opt.right.label [b3c370] = 猜一个
# en: "Energy follows intention." His eyebrows twitch. "Acceptable." The room exhales.
opt.right.say.1 [a4daea] = “能量追随意念。”他的眉毛抽动了一下。“可以接受。”全班松了口气。
# en: Your guess is so wrong the student next to you gasps. Thorne simply says, "No," and moves on.
opt.right.say.2 [0a5012] = 你猜得错得离谱，旁边的同学倒吸一口冷气。索恩只说了一句“不对”，就继续讲下去了。

@event thorne_office_hours
# en: Office Hours
title [2f554a] = 答疑时间
# en: Thorne stops you after class. "Your casting is sloppy and your instincts are good. That's an annoying combination. Thursdays. Seven o'clock. My office. Don't be late."
text [e4245b] = 下课后索恩叫住了你。“你的施法很马虎，直觉却很好。这是个恼人的组合。周四。七点。我的办公室。别迟到。”
# en: A cramped office full of scorched books and a single lit candle, a stern professor leaning back in his chair, fingers steepled.
scene [78fbf0] = 一间堆满烧焦书本、只点着一支蜡烛的狭小办公室，严厉的教授靠在椅背上，十指相抵。
# en: Politely decline — you're stretched thin
opt.left.label [d714b1] = 礼貌地拒绝——你已经分身乏术
# en: "Hm." He seems neither surprised nor pleased. Thorne is rarely either.
opt.left.say.1 [c8eaad] = “嗯。”他看起来既不意外，也不高兴。索恩很少有这两种情绪。
# en: Be there at seven
opt.right.label [5fe202] = 七点准时到
# en: Two hours of brutal drills. At the end, he hands you a book from his own shelf. "Read it. Return it unburnt."
opt.right.say.1 [80a8e2] = 两个小时残酷的操练。结束时，他从自己的书架上抽出一本书递给你。“读完。还的时候别烧着。”

@event thorne_storm_story
# en: The Storm Duel
title [c9a5ed] = 风暴决斗
# en: During a thunderstorm, Thorne stops mid-lecture and watches the lightning. "They say I out-dueled a storm once," he says, to nobody in particular. "Would you like to know what actually happened?"
text [1d58d7] = 雷雨中，索恩讲到一半停了下来，望着窗外的闪电。“他们说我曾经在决斗中赢过一场风暴，”他说，不知是对谁说的，“想知道真正发生了什么吗？”
# en: An old professor standing at a rain-lashed window, lightning illuminating a long scar along his jaw.
scene [3aa02a] = 一位年迈的教授站在被雨水抽打的窗前，闪电照亮了他下颌上一道长长的伤疤。
# en: "Yes, sir."
opt.left.label [ad622a] = “想，教授。”
# en: He lost, he says. Badly. He spent a year learning why. "Losing well," he says, "is the only thing worth teaching." The class is silent.
opt.left.say.1 [bd0455] = 他说，他输了。输得很惨。他花了一年才弄明白为什么。“输得漂亮，”他说，“是唯一值得教的东西。”全班鸦雀无声。
# en: Stay quiet
opt.right.label [9adbd8] = 保持沉默
# en: He shakes his head and returns to the lecture. You'll always wonder.
opt.right.say.1 [90167f] = 他摇摇头，继续讲课。你会一直好奇下去。

@event thorne_recommendation
# en: A Letter of Recommendation
title [c8fd60] = 推荐信
# en: Thorne calls you to his office and slides an envelope across the desk. "The Conclave asked for my recommendations. I wrote one. I don't write many." He pauses. "Don't make me regret it."
text [126063] = 索恩把你叫到办公室，把一个信封推过桌面。“议会请我写推荐信。我写了一封。我很少写。”他顿了顿，“别让我后悔。”
# en: A wax-sealed envelope on a professor's desk with a student's name written on it in sharp, angular handwriting.
scene [96717b] = 教授桌上一个封着火漆的信封，上面用锋利棱角的字迹写着一个学生的名字。
# en: Thank him sincerely
opt.left.label [028201] = 真诚地道谢
# en: "Go away," he says gruffly. "I have marking." You see him smile at the window as you leave.
opt.left.say.1 [91553f] = “走吧，”他粗声说，“我还要批作业。”你离开时，看见他对着窗户笑了。
# en: Ask why you
opt.right.label [ca1833] = 问为什么是你
# en: "Because you ask questions like that," he says. "Most students don't. Go." You leave unsure whether you were praised or dismissed.
opt.right.say.1 [52bd7f] = “因为你会问这种问题，”他说，“大多数学生不会。走吧。”你离开时也说不清自己是被夸了还是被打发了。

@event thorne_disappointed
# en: A Word in Private
title [ff3088] = 私下谈谈
# en: Thorne holds up your last three essays. All red. "You're better than this," he says. "That's not a compliment. It's an accusation."
text [cc601d] = 索恩举起你最近的三篇论文。全是红的。“你不止这个水平，”他说，“这不是夸奖。是指控。”
# en: A professor standing by his desk with a sheaf of red-marked papers, a student standing awkwardly before him.
scene [9d745e] = 一位教授站在桌旁，手持一沓满是红批的论文，一个学生尴尬地站在他面前。
# en: Make excuses
opt.left.label [271029] = 找借口
# en: He listens to them all and says nothing. The silence is the worst grade yet.
opt.left.say.1 [f08449] = 他听完了你所有的借口，一言不发。这份沉默是你得过最差的分数。
# en: Ask for help
opt.right.label [e11804] = 请求帮助
# en: He sighs and pulls out a chair. "Sit. We'll start with the first essay, and we'll stay until it's right." You stay until midnight.
opt.right.say.1 [0a15d2] = 他叹了口气，拉出一把椅子。“坐。我们从第一篇开始，改到对为止。”你们一直改到半夜。

@event maud_chickens
# en: The Great Chicken Escape
title [c0698d] = 鸡群大逃亡
# en: Forty chickens are loose on the main lawn, pursued by an old woman in a straw hat. "Don't just stand there, dearie!" she shouts at you. "Grab the speckled one, she's the ringleader!"
text [c7632d] = 四十只鸡在大草坪上四处逃窜，一位戴草帽的老妇人在后面追。“别光站着呀，孩子！”她冲你喊，“抓那只带斑点的，她是头儿！”
# en: Chickens fleeing across a lawn in every direction, an old woman in a straw hat waving a broom, students diving after birds.
scene [f345a3] = 鸡群在草坪上四散奔逃，戴草帽的老妇人挥着扫帚，学生们扑向鸡群。
# en: Keep walking
opt.left.label [6ca967] = 继续走你的路
# en: You hear a crash, a squawk and a triumphant cackle behind you. The chickens, it seems, are caught.
opt.left.say.1 [62bfac] = 你听见身后一声巨响、一声鸡叫和一阵得意的笑。看来鸡都被抓住了。
# en: Grab the speckled one
opt.right.label [5c1b61] = 抓住那只带斑点的
# en: You tackle the ringleader. The rest give up. "Good hands," says Old Maud, pressing a warm egg into your palm. "Come for tea."
opt.right.say.1 [a339b6] = 你扑倒了头儿。其余的都放弃了。“好身手。”老莫德说着把一枚温热的鸡蛋塞进你手心，“来喝茶吧。”
# en: The ringleader escapes and pecks you, but Maud is impressed by your enthusiasm. "Come for tea. Bring plasters."
opt.right.say.2 [bfdfbf] = 头儿逃走了还啄了你一口，但莫德很欣赏你的热情。“来喝茶吧。带上创可贴。”

@event maud_honey
# en: Honey for a Cold
title [b7cd42] = 治感冒的蜂蜜
# en: Maud spots you sniffling across the lawn and drags you into her cottage. "Sit," she orders, pouring honey into something steaming that smells of lemon and thunder.
text [7490d5] = 莫德隔着草坪看见你在吸鼻子，把你拽进了她的小屋。“坐下。”她命令道，把蜂蜜倒进一杯冒着热气、闻起来像柠檬和雷声的东西里。
# en: A small cottage kitchen with bundles of herbs hanging from the beams, an old woman pouring golden honey into a steaming mug.
scene [eeaeed] = 小屋厨房的房梁上挂着一捆捆草药，老妇人正把金色的蜂蜜倒进一只冒热气的杯子。
# en: Drink it all
opt.left.label [06ea01] = 一饮而尽
# en: It tastes like summer and lightning. You sneeze sparks for the rest of the day. By morning you're cured and slightly glowing.
opt.left.say.1 [2d602b] = 它尝起来像夏天和闪电。你一整天都在打喷嚏，喷出小火星。第二天早上你就好了，身上还微微发光。
# en: Drink it and help with chores
opt.right.label [cbf3a4] = 边喝边帮她干活
# en: You sip and sort herbs while she tells you the names of every plant in the room. You remember most of them.
opt.right.say.1 [d8a82c] = 你一边小口喝着，一边分拣草药，她把屋里每一株植物的名字都告诉了你。你记住了大半。

@event maud_old_student
# en: Maud Was a Student Once
title [bad37c] = 莫德曾经也是学生
# en: "I was a student here, you know," Maud says, watching the lake. "Sixty years ago. The lake froze one spring. Three of my friends went down to the boathouse that night. Only two came back." She doesn't look at you. "Ask me what I know."
text [eef642] = “你知道吗，我以前也是这里的学生，”莫德望着湖面说，“六十年前。有一年春天，湖结冰了。那天夜里，我的三个朋友下到了船屋。只回来了两个。”她没有看你。“问我知道些什么吧。”
# en: An old woman sitting on a bench by the lake at dusk, looking at the water as if it might look back.
scene [89e70b] = 黄昏时分，一位老妇人坐在湖边长椅上，望着湖水，仿佛湖水也会回望她。
# en: "You don't have to tell me."
opt.left.label [194cf6] = “您不必告诉我的。”
# en: She pats your hand. "Kind. But time's short, dearie." She tells you anyway, a little at a time, over many cups of tea.
opt.left.say.1 [9b1d22] = 她拍了拍你的手。“好孩子。可时间不多了。”她还是告诉了你，一点一点地，就着许多杯茶。
# en: "What do you know?"
opt.right.label [099f17] = “您知道些什么？”
# en: "Seven locks, one in each tower. The key's a star that eats light. And the thing below loves a lonely heart." She finally looks at you. "Don't be lonely."
opt.right.say.1 [737ddb] = “七把锁，每座塔里一把。钥匙是一颗吞噬光的星。而下面那个东西，最爱孤独的心。”她终于看向你。“别孤单。”

@event maud_bees
# en: The Silver Bees
title [1eab66] = 银蜂
# en: "The silver bees need moving to the summer meadow," Maud says, handing you a veiled hat. "They're friendly. Mostly. Don't make any sudden thoughts."
text [30a86a] = “银蜂要搬去夏季草场了，”莫德说着递给你一顶带面纱的帽子，“它们很友好。大体上。别突然冒出什么念头就行。”
# en: Wooden hives in a wildflower meadow, an old woman in a veiled hat lifting a frame dripping with silver honey, bees glinting in the sun.
scene [53eac5] = 野花草场上的木蜂箱，一位戴面纱帽的老妇人举起一框滴着银色蜂蜜的巢脾，蜜蜂在阳光下闪闪发亮。
# en: Help with the hives
opt.left.label [05ba5e] = 帮忙搬蜂箱
# en: The bees hum around you like a blessing. Maud gives you a jar of silver honey that sells for eight crowns. You eat half first.
opt.left.say.1 [6e9b07] = 蜜蜂围着你嗡嗡作响，像一种祝福。莫德给了你一罐能卖八克朗的银蜜。你先吃了一半。
# en: You have a sudden thought. The bees know. You spend the evening with vinegar on your stings.
opt.left.say.2 [8b74be] = 你突然冒出了一个念头。蜜蜂知道了。你整晚都在往蜇伤上抹醋。
# en: Watch from a safe distance
opt.right.label [5c0ef7] = 在安全距离外观看
# en: You watch Maud move hives barehanded, singing to them. It's the calmest you've felt all month.
opt.right.say.1 [fca1ee] = 你看着莫德赤手搬动蜂箱，一边对它们唱歌。这是你这个月最平静的时刻。

@event maud_ill
# en: Maud Is Unwell
title [1570b9] = 莫德病了
# en: Maud's chickens are running wild, unfed. You find her in bed, grey-faced and coughing. "Just a chill," she wheezes. "I'm eighty-one. I'm allowed."
text [d16f4b] = 莫德的鸡没人喂，满地乱跑。你发现她躺在床上，脸色灰白，咳个不停。“只是着了点凉，”她喘着气说，“我八十一了。有这个资格。”
# en: A small cottage bedroom with a patchwork quilt, an old woman propped up on pillows, a student reading aloud by candlelight.
scene [a2af84] = 小屋卧室里铺着拼布被，一位老妇人靠在枕头上，一个学生在烛光下为她读报。
# en: Fetch Sister Amaranth
opt.left.label [0ebdc9] = 去叫阿玛兰斯修女
# en: Amaranth brings tonics and a stern lecture. Maud is back on her feet in a week, grumbling about fuss.
opt.left.say.1 [79a7ad] = 阿玛兰斯带来了药剂和一通严厉的训话。一周后莫德就下了床，嘟囔着大家小题大做。
# en: Look after her yourself for a week
opt.right.label [c0447c] = 亲自照顾她一周
# en: You feed chickens, brew teas, read her the newspaper. When she's well, she gives you a sprig of rosemary. "You'll do," she says. "You'll do."
opt.right.say.1 [4fecac] = 你喂鸡、煮茶、给她读报纸。她康复后，给了你一枝迷迭香。“你行，”她说，“你行的。”

@event isolde_intro
# en: She Knows Your Name
title [9a7a2b] = 她知道你的名字
# en: At dinner, a cool hand rests on the back of your chair. The headmistress. "{player}," she says, though you've never met. "Your marks in Arcana are interesting. Your marks in punctuality, less so." She moves on.
text [0b5a32] = 晚餐时，一只微凉的手搭在你的椅背上。是院长。“{player}，”她说，尽管你们从未见过，“你的奥术成绩很有意思。你的守时成绩，就没那么有意思了。”她继续往前走了。
# en: A tall pale woman in dark robes pausing behind a student's chair in a candlelit dining hall, a hand resting lightly on the chair back.
scene [b2fa1a] = 烛光摇曳的餐厅里，一位身着深色长袍的高挑苍白女子在一名学生的椅子后驻足，一只手轻轻搭在椅背上。
# en: Stammer an apology
opt.left.label [d97a4c] = 结结巴巴地道歉
# en: She's already three tables away. Every student between you sits a little straighter.
opt.left.say.1 [e1b364] = 她已经走出三张桌子远了。你们之间的每个学生都坐直了一点。
# en: "Interesting how, Headmistress?"
opt.right.label [836bca] = “怎么个有意思法，院长？”
# en: She pauses. Turns. Almost smiles. "Ask me again at the end of your first year," she says. The table stares at you.
opt.right.say.1 [912689] = 她停下脚步。转身。几乎笑了。“等你一年级结束时再问我一次。”她说。整桌人都盯着你看。

@event isolde_tea
# en: Tea in the Tower
title [b7137e] = 塔楼下午茶
# en: An invitation to tea with the headmistress. Students talk about these the way soldiers talk about battles. She pours. "Tell me, {player}: what do you want to become?"
text [9726d0] = 一份与院长共进下午茶的邀请。学生们谈论这种事，就像士兵谈论战役。她倒着茶。“告诉我，{player}：你想成为什么样的人？”
# en: A round tower study at twilight, two delicate teacups on a small table, a headmistress pouring tea with a perfectly steady hand.
scene [71ceab] = 暮色中的圆形塔楼书房，小桌上两只精致的茶杯，院长倒茶的手稳得纹丝不动。
# en: Give an ambitious answer
opt.left.label [aa3b70] = 给一个雄心勃勃的回答
# en: She listens without interrupting, then says, "Good. Ambition without arrogance. Rarer than you'd think."
opt.left.say.1 [7c5144] = 她一句也没打断地听完，然后说：“很好。有雄心而不傲慢。比你想象的要少见。”
# en: She nods politely. "Ambition is a fine servant," she says, "and a poor master." You're dismissed shortly after.
opt.left.say.2 [7dba0b] = 她礼貌地点点头。“雄心是个好仆人，”她说，“却是个坏主人。”没过多久你就被请走了。
# en: Admit you don't know yet
opt.right.label [0c2530] = 承认你还不知道
# en: "Neither did I, at your age," she says. "I still don't, some days. That's the point of an academy." She refills your cup.
opt.right.say.1 [80f029] = “我在你这个年纪时也不知道，”她说，“有些日子我现在也不知道。这正是学院存在的意义。”她为你续上了茶。

@event isolde_warning
# en: A Quiet Warning
title [a5c708] = 一句轻声的警告
# en: The headmistress falls into step beside you in the colonnade. "I hear your name more often than I'd like," she says pleasantly. "In the wrong rooms. I'd hate to hear it in mine."
text [01291a] = 院长在柱廊里走到你身边，与你并肩而行。“我听到你名字的次数比我希望的要多，”她和气地说，“在不该听到的房间里。我可不想在我的房间里听到它。”
# en: A headmistress walking alongside a student in a long colonnade, hands clasped behind her back, speaking without looking at them.
scene [052fbe] = 长长的柱廊里，院长背着手与一名学生并肩而行，说话时并不看对方。
# en: Promise to do better
opt.left.label [cba502] = 保证会改
# en: "Good." She stops walking. You keep going. When you look back, she's gone.
opt.left.say.1 [b48ece] = “很好。”她停下脚步。你继续往前走。回头时，她已经不见了。
# en: Defend yourself
opt.right.label [b9d2ca] = 为自己辩护
# en: You lay it out plainly. She listens, then nods once. "Fair. I'll have a word with certain prefects."
opt.right.say.1 [72ff59] = 你把事情原原本本讲清楚。她听完，点了一下头。“公道。我会找某些级长谈谈。”
# en: "Hm," she says. "Let's hope you're right." It doesn't feel like hope.
opt.right.say.2 [d3a208] = “嗯，”她说，“但愿你是对的。”这听起来可不像但愿。

@event vey_intro
# en: Tea That Isn't There
title [52dadd] = 不存在的茶
# en: First Illusion lecture. Professor Vey pours you a cup of tea from a pot you would swear is empty, and waits. "Milk?" she asks. The whole row turns to see what you'll do with a cup of nothing.
text [e330e1] = 第一节幻术课。维伊教授从一只你敢发誓是空的茶壶里给你倒了一杯茶，然后等着。“加奶吗？”她问。整排人都转过头来，看你怎么对付一杯什么都没有的茶。
# en: A lecture room hung with velvet curtains, a woman in a violet coat pouring from an empty teapot into a student's empty cup.
scene [7245af] = 挂着天鹅绒帘子的教室里，一个穿紫罗兰色外套的女人从空茶壶往学生的空杯子里倒茶。
# en: Drink it, and thank her
opt.left.label [374044] = 喝下去，再道谢
# en: You sip, sigh and ask where she buys it. Vey's mouth twitches. "Lapsang. There was never any tea, of course. Sit down; you'll do."
opt.left.say.1 [5466bf] = 你抿一口，叹口气，问她在哪儿买的。维伊的嘴角抽动了一下。“正山小种。当然，从来就没有茶。坐吧，你行。”
# en: You raise the cup with a flourish and tip it a little too far. Nothing pours out, and the whole row sees nothing pour out. Vey writes something down, and smiles at it.
opt.left.say.2 [2dbeaf] = 你潇洒地举起杯子，却倾得太过了。什么也没倒出来，而整排人都看见什么也没倒出来。维伊记了点什么，对着它笑了。
# en: Say the cup is empty
opt.right.label [9ea330] = 说杯子是空的
# en: "It's empty," you say. "So it is," says Vey, pleased and disappointed at once. "Honest eyes. We shall have to do something about those."
opt.right.say.1 [73d780] = “是空的，”你说。“确实，”维伊说，既满意又失望。“诚实的眼睛。我们得想办法治一治。”

@event brask_intro
# en: Shovel. There. Go.
title [ee049c] = 铲子。那儿。去。
# en: First Beastcraft lesson, at the stables. Professor Brask is explaining to a hippogriff, in full and courteous sentences, that the new students will be clumsy and she is to be patient with them. Then she turns to you. "Shovel. There. Go."
text [dc2351] = 第一节驭兽课，在马厩。布拉斯克教授正用完整而客气的句子向一头鹰头马身有翼兽解释：新生会笨手笨脚，请它多担待。然后她转向你。“铲子。那儿。去。”
# en: A long stable in morning light, a grey-haired professor talking earnestly to a hippogriff while a student stands holding a shovel.
scene [98b211] = 晨光中长长的马厩，一位灰发教授正认真地对一头鹰头马身有翼兽说话，一个学生拿着铲子站在一旁。
# en: Muck out without a word
opt.left.label [ef11b2] = 一声不吭地铲
# en: You shovel until your arms shake. Brask watches, then tells the hippogriff, loud enough for you to hear, "This one might do." To you she says nothing, which you later learn is praise.
opt.left.say.1 [2284b5] = 你铲到胳膊发抖。布拉斯克看着，然后对鹰头马身有翼兽说，声音大得刚好让你听见：“这个兴许行。”她对你什么也没说——后来你才知道，那就是夸奖。
# en: Ask what today's lesson is
opt.right.label [068c9f] = 问今天学什么
# en: Brask tells the hippogriff a story about a student who asked questions before shovelling. It ends with a bite. "Moral: shovel." You shovel, a little behind the others.
opt.right.say.1 [af14ce] = 布拉斯克给鹰头马身有翼兽讲了个故事：有个学生总在铲粪之前提问。结尾是被咬了一口。“寓意：铲。”你开始铲，比别人慢了一步。

@event pell_first_shift
# en: Count Aloud
title [39b25b] = 数出声来
# en: Your first shift at Pell & Daughters. Old Pell climbs down from his ladder, hands you a dropper and a bottle of tincture, and points at a waiting customer. "Twelve drops," he says. "Aloud. Everyone counts aloud in this shop. The drawers like it."
text [e01d70] = 你在佩尔父女药铺的第一个班。老佩尔从梯子上爬下来，递给你一支滴管和一瓶酊剂，指了指一位等着的顾客。“十二滴，”他说，“数出声。这店里人人都数出声。抽屉们喜欢听。”
# en: A narrow apothecary lined with tiny labelled drawers, an old man on a ladder holding out a glass dropper to a nervous new clerk.
scene [9281b1] = 一间狭长的药铺，墙上满是贴着标签的小抽屉，梯子上的老人向一个紧张的新店员递过一支玻璃滴管。
# en: Count every drop aloud
opt.left.label [2046bb] = 每一滴都数出声
# en: "One. Two. Three." Your voice fills the shop; the customer joins in at nine. Pell nods once. "Twelve. Not eleven. Not thirteen. You'll count like that until they bury you."
opt.left.say.1 [5a7443] = “一。二。三。”你的声音充满了整间铺子；数到九时顾客也跟着数。佩尔点了一下头。“十二。不是十一，不是十三。你就这么数，一直数到入土。”
# en: Count in your head, quickly
opt.right.label [585870] = 在心里快快地数
# en: Twelve drops, done in a breath; the customer tells the whole queue how quick the new clerk is. Pell counts the level against the light. "Correct. Next time, aloud. I like to hear a thing being right."
opt.right.say.1 [95b946] = 十二滴，一口气滴完；顾客跟整条队的人夸新店员手快。佩尔把瓶子举到光下看刻度。“对。下次数出声。我喜欢听见事情做对的声音。”
# en: You lose count at eight and guess. Pell tips the bottle out and starts it again, aloud, without a word to you. The customer leaves with the right dose and a look at you.
opt.right.say.2 [2e54e1] = 数到八你就数乱了，只好估。佩尔把瓶子倒空，重新数了一遍，出声地数，一句话也没对你说。顾客拿着正确的剂量走了，临走看了你一眼。
